IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `maia-dates`
IMPORT `maia-benefits`

-- Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in maia-benefits.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates and amounts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the date`

`driver` MEANS `I was the driver of a vehicle involved`
`owner` MEANS `I owned a vehicle involved but was not driving it`
`neither` MEANS `I was neither the owner nor the driver of a vehicle involved`

-- The accident in most cases: Friday 1 March 2024. Day 1 is 2 March 2024; day 91 is 31 May 2024; day 92 is 1 June
-- 2024; day 182 (26 weeks) is 30 August 2024; day 364 (52 weeks) is 28 February 2025; day 546 (78 weeks) is
-- 29 August 2025; day 728 (104 weeks) is 27 February 2026; day 1092 (156 weeks) is 26 February 2027; day 1820
-- (260 weeks) is 23 February 2029.
`A` MEANS `d` 1 3 2024

§§ `s 1.6, Regulation cl 4 -- threshold injuries`

#ASSERT `Is my injury a threshold injury` `an injury to soft tissue (muscle, tendon, ligament, meniscus, cartilage, fascia, fibrous tissue, fat, blood vessel, synovial membrane) that is not a rupture` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my injury a threshold injury` `a complete or partial rupture of a tendon, ligament, meniscus or cartilage` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my injury a threshold injury` `an injury to a nerve, other than a spinal nerve root` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my injury a threshold injury` `an injury to a spinal nerve root showing neurological signs other than radiculopathy` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my injury a threshold injury` `an injury to a spinal nerve root with radiculopathy` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my injury a threshold injury` `acute stress disorder or adjustment disorder` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my injury a threshold injury` `another psychological or psychiatric injury that is not a recognised psychiatric illness` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my injury a threshold injury` `a recognised psychiatric illness` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my injury a threshold injury` `a fracture, or another injury not listed` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 1.8-1.10, 3.1, 3.35, 3.36, 3.37 -- are statutory benefits payable at all`

-- Arguments: NSW; after commencement; caused during driving etc; gradual; cover; work injury claim; workers comp payable;
-- role; fault %; uninsured; authority; grounds to believe uninsured; charged; acquitted.
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `neither` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `neither` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `neither` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `neither` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `neither` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1.10: no cover and no work injury claim; a work injury claim alone suffices.
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `neither` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `neither` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3.35(1): workers compensation payable.
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `neither` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3.36: a driver 62% at fault of an uninsured vehicle, with authority and no grounds (s 3.36(5)): payable.
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `driver` 62 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Without authority: not payable. With grounds to believe it uninsured: not payable.
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `driver` 62 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `driver` 62 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 61% is not "greater than 61%": payable.
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `driver` 61 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An owner not driving gets no s 3.36(5) protection.
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `owner` 100 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The driver's vehicle was insured: payable even wholly at fault (s 3.1(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `driver` 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A pedestrian wholly at fault: s 3.36 does not reach them.
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `neither` 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3.37: charged and not acquitted; acquitted.
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `driver` 30 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are statutory benefits payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `driver` 30 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 3.2 -- who pays`

-- Arguments: vehicles; cover; licensed; policy covers statutory benefits; Authority approved; T&C after 5 years; LTCS agreed.
#ASSERT `Who pays my statutory benefits` 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the insurer of the motor vehicle`
#ASSERT `Who pays my statutory benefits` 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the Nominal Defendant`
#ASSERT `Who pays my statutory benefits` 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the insurer of the motor vehicle`
#ASSERT `Who pays my statutory benefits` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the insurer of the at-fault motor vehicle`
#ASSERT `Who pays my statutory benefits` 3 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the Nominal Defendant`
#ASSERT `Who pays my statutory benefits` 2 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the Nominal Defendant`
#ASSERT `Who pays my statutory benefits` 2 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `a licensed insurer, under arrangements the Authority approved`
#ASSERT `Who pays my statutory benefits` 2 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the Nominal Defendant, on behalf of the non-licensed insurer`
#ASSERT `Who pays my statutory benefits` 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the Lifetime Care and Support Authority`
#ASSERT `Who pays my statutory benefits` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the Lifetime Care and Support Authority`
#ASSERT `Who pays my statutory benefits` 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

